  "id": "COMPOUND:2248 - PROTEIN:6294",
  "verbalization": "Myricetin, a flavonoid, is shown to interact with the Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6 (EPPE6) through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Myricetin acts as a target for several compounds, including the Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase and Peripheral myelin protein 22, which in turn target EPPE6. This indicates a potential mechanism where Myricetin may influence the activity of these proteins, which are involved in nucleotide metabolism and cellular processes. The presence of multiple distinct targets for Myricetin, each leading to EPPE6, suggests a broader role in modulating the function of this enzyme family. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Myricetin could exert its effects through a complex network of interactions, possibly involving the regulation of nucleotide metabolism and cellular stress responses. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Myricetin and EPPE6, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
